  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Offer four unique noun forms only, never full sentences or extra words.",
      "Exactly one choice is correct; never write two forms that can both fit the stem.",
      "Keep the wrong form from the stem as one distractor.",
      "Prefer this set when it fits: singular, plural, singular possessive, plural possessive.",
      "For irregular plurals include a common misspelling such as childrens.",
      "Tier 1 distractors are far: plain singular versus a clear plural or a missing 's.",
      "Tier 3 distractors are near-miss possessives of the other number, such as dog's versus dogs'.",
      "Kid world only: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather. No brands.",
      "Use <NAME> for people; never write a real first name."
    ]
  },
